            {
                "entry_id": "3b328dc3-f6ca-3a94-b306-c8451d713d26",
                "word": "pandy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1b3319e4-7b8a-4f70-a1dd-e80248f62767",
                        "entry_id": "3b328dc3-f6ca-3a94-b306-c8451d713d26",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pandies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f2b651b9-ad66-3f4f-8696-d2a2c6beffad",
                        "entry_id": "3b328dc3-f6ca-3a94-b306-c8451d713d26",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mutineer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ce993e1-d52e-4ab8-b4f0-3cce9c07c811",
                                "sense_id": "f2b651b9-ad66-3f4f-8696-d2a2c6beffad",
                                "text": "As long as I feel the entire confidence I do, that we shall triumph over this iniquitous combination, I cannot feel gloom. I leave this feeling to the Pandies, who have sacrificed honour and existence to the ghost of a delusion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdb04747-0f83-413d-8cee-19339a969061",
                                "sense_id": "f2b651b9-ad66-3f4f-8696-d2a2c6beffad",
                                "text": "We had not long to wait before the line of guns, howitzers, and mortar carts, chiefly drawn by elephants, soon hove in sight... Poor Pandy, what a pounding was in store for you!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d966ba55-fb3f-4afa-99b3-454a90f890f0",
                                "sense_id": "f2b651b9-ad66-3f4f-8696-d2a2c6beffad",
                                "text": "But, as my friend Dennis Dolbear has pointed out, if Flashy were truly the Utter Bastard he wants to paint himself/see himself as, after they got him down off the muzzle of that gun, he'd have gone \"Right -- where's the Surgeon for my broken arm and the Officer's Mess for a quick gin or two? Oh, and carry on the good work, Lieutenant.\" and walked away not paying a bit of attention as the other pandies were blown from the guns."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79364697-154b-4162-9246-6f761133b4f6",
                                "sense_id": "f2b651b9-ad66-3f4f-8696-d2a2c6beffad",
                                "text": "The manu guy in one of his reply to madurai veeran said that all pandies would have been \"iruddu\" pandies if not for the Namboodries, his obvious reference to the Brahmin blood lightning the dark colour of the original Dark Dravidian Tamils."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8a05343-d4a2-4501-982c-1df79b88b4a9",
                                "sense_id": "f2b651b9-ad66-3f4f-8696-d2a2c6beffad",
                                "text": "He blew forty prisoners from the mouths of his cannon to make the damn pandies understand the fate that awaits them."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "26d5c7c8-2dcb-3b7c-bc82-641cf689d654",
                "word": "Pandy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f1287cb3-6928-47d8-ac27-42a98a85d7a2",
                        "entry_id": "26d5c7c8-2dcb-3b7c-bc82-641cf689d654",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Pandies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a3ab0116-6f28-3e76-803c-8b0780cefe7e",
                        "entry_id": "26d5c7c8-2dcb-3b7c-bc82-641cf689d654",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of pandy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "353f196e-42dd-449b-a9cc-c918d05fcad0",
                                "sense_id": "a3ab0116-6f28-3e76-803c-8b0780cefe7e",
                                "text": "And as I said, sir, the whole garden was swarming wi' Pandies, so have a care."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8745d0e6-fbd3-49e9-838e-cb5e6ee8585a",
                                "sense_id": "a3ab0116-6f28-3e76-803c-8b0780cefe7e",
                                "text": "We had not evacuated the Martiniére fifteen minutes today before it was swarming with Pandies like a nest of ants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e3470e7-1cbc-416c-85ae-06b1238a3c5a",
                                "sense_id": "a3ab0116-6f28-3e76-803c-8b0780cefe7e",
                                "text": "Many a morning before breakfast I was present here and assisted to hang a dozen or more of the rebel Pandies on the branches."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "81afa6e5-584d-352c-857c-2a4dcc8c4e74",
                "word": "pandy",
                "pos": "verb",
